await writeFile(new URL('index.html', import.meta.url), `<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="color-scheme" content="light"><title>Five directions · Ritua Identity & Goals</title><style>${baseCss}\n${galleryCss}</style></head><body><main class="gallery"><div class="gallery-head"><img src="${logoUrl}" alt="">Ritua <span style="font-weight:400;margin-left:8px">Design exploration</span></div><h1>Five directions for Identity & Goals.</h1><p class="gallery-intro">Explore five ways to connect who you want to become with what you want to accomplish. Open a concept to try its interactions, then switch between directions from the toolbar.</p><div class="gallery-meta"><span>5 standalone HTML prototypes</span><span>Ritua’s existing visual language</span><span>Example content · No account needed</span></div><div class="gallery-grid">${concepts.map((concept,i)=>`<a class="concept-card" href="${concept.file}"><div class="preview-frame"><img src="previews/${concept.file.replace('.html','.jpg')}" alt="Preview of ${concept.name}" loading="eager"></div><div class="card-heading"><h2><span class="concept-number">0${i+1}</span>${concept.name}</h2>${icons.ArrowUpRight}</div><p>${concept.description}</p></a>`).join('')}</div><div class="gallery-footer"><strong>Try it, don’t just look at it.</strong> Edit an intention, add a goal, move an ambition between horizons, update a result, or write a reflection. Edits stay in the open page; the reset button restores the example.<br>These are design concepts. They don’t read or modify your Ritua workspace.</div></main></body></html>`)

await writeFile(new URL('README.md', import.meta.url), `# Ritua · Identity & Goals concepts\n\nFive standalone, offline HTML concepts grounded in the current production UI. Open index.html to compare them, or open any concept directly. Every concept embeds its CSS, JavaScript, Ritua logo and Phosphor icons. Preview images are used only by the gallery.\n\n## Directions\n\n${concepts.map((c,i)=>`${i+1}. **${c.name}** — ${c.description} (${c.file})`).join('\n')}\n\n## Prototype behavior\n\n- Sample data is isolated from the application; no production modules import these concepts.\n- Changes live in page memory and reset when reloaded.\n- No AI integration, account, analytics, network requests, or durable application storage.\n- Identity is user-authored and mutable. Progress applies to outcomes, never to a person’s identity.\n- In the goal workspace, confirming a practice and updating an outcome are separate actions.\n- Example dates are anchored to September 30, 2026.\n\n## Regenerate\n\nFrom the repository root: node design/identity-goals/generate.mjs\n\nThe generator uses existing React and Phosphor packages only at build time. Generated pages require no packages.\n`)

